{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BOTH CHANGES ARE NOW ON GERRIT AS A STACK, so the ordering criterion is enforced by the dependency graph rather than by my discipline alone.\n\n    1327  eb6e: point the review bot at Bedrock      <- THE FLIP (child)     Change-Id I837be12fbe2b3b810947128f2a1680b9ab3e83ad\n    1326  eb6e: Bedrock safety net and packaging     <- SAFETY NET (parent)  Change-Id I9762105851d88e6e6d02ef68d06c195c91602ad9\nConfirmed via Gerrit's own related-changes endpoint, not inferred from my local history. 1327 cannot merge before 1326.\n\nVOTE STATE at time of writing: 1326 LLM-Review=+1, Verified pending; 1327 both pending (just pushed); 1325 (the drill/comparison fixture) LLM-Review=+1 AND Verified=+1, i.e. fully green and deliberately NOT submitted.\n\nCHANGE 1327 EVIDENCE, all by exit code with the tree asserted clean beforehand.\nFull non-integration suite on 047764d528: 9631 passed, 34 skipped, 0 failed, 21m23s, exit 0, git status --porcelain empty.\nThen REBASED onto 1326's pushed revision 01aab994fe (my stack had been built on the pre-amend c8d1685bb1; pushing without rebasing would have created a STALE SECOND PATCHSET on 1326 carrying older content — worth stating because the failure would have looked like a successful push). Result fbe1c1476c, Change-Id preserved, parent verified as 01aab994fe, and 'git diff 047764d528 HEAD' shows ONLY the inherited monitoring_eb6e.tf comment — my own content is byte-identical across the rebase.\nRe-run against the rebased tree fbe1c1476c: the 4-assertion pinning test 4 passed exit 0, make lint 0, make typecheck 0, scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py 0, scripts/check_config_reads.py 0, scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check 0, terraform fmt -check -recursive 0, terraform validate 0.\n\nSTATED EXCEPTION, not a green gate: the FULL pytest suite was not re-run after the rebase. The delta is a six-line comment inside infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf in the PARENT commit; no .py, .yml or .toml file differs. I did not rely on that argument alone — the one test in my change that actually READS infra/terraform/*.tf (the alarm/ModelId pin) was re-run against the rebased tree and passes, and I confirmed the new comment text introduces no 'ModelId = \"...\"' string that could perturb its regex. Recording this because 'the suite passed' and 'the suite passed on the artifact I pushed' are different claims and the second is the one that matters.\n\nTWO ENVIRONMENT NOTES worth carrying. (1) 'terraform validate' first failed exit 1 in this worktree with 'no package for registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/random 3.9.0 cached in .terraform/providers'. That is a MISSING terraform init in a fresh worktree, not a configuration error — 'terraform init -backend=false' then validate exits 0 ('Success! The configuration is valid'), and -backend=false is sufficient because validate needs no state. A fresh worktree will reproduce this every time. (2) CORRECTION TO THE INHERITED HANDOFF: it states that 'make lint also runs a COMMENT-HYGIENE check'. IT DOES NOT in this tree — the Makefile contains no reference to it; it is a separate CI step at .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml running scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py. Anyone relying on make lint to cover comment hygiene is not running it. I ran it explicitly on both changes: exit 0.\n\nuv.lock UNTOUCHED and verified sufficient for the added extra, from the authoring agent's captured output: 'uv lock --check' exit 0 (Resolved 167 packages), and 'uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra reviewbot --extra bedrock --dry-run' exit 0 with 'Found up-to-date lockfile at: uv.lock' and no drift complaint. So the Dockerfile's --locked install is satisfied by the committed lock and no regeneration is part of this story.\n\nNEXT, in this order, and nothing is flipped until each prior step is observed: 1326 reaches Verified +1 -> submit 1326 -> terraform apply (the alarm; apply path and credentials already proven) -> record the alarm ARN, a forced notification, and a NON-INSUFFICIENT_DATA state after an evaluation period -> run the pre-registered induced-VOTER_ERROR drill while the bot is still on Anthropic -> only then submit 1327 and let autodeploy (2-minute timer, rebuilds on source change, defers while a review is in flight) carry the cutover -> post-cutover vote, usage-log tally, provenance comparison against the recorded findings A, denied-access drill, kill switch end-to-end."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785799492903825001,"uuid":"3a0a565f-2cca-4c40-bd6d-77adae2b715b"}